# Vendored third-party libraries are bytes, not text.
#
# `public/vendor/xlsx.full.min.js` is a copy of a specific published SheetJS
# release, and it is the fallback readers get when cdn.sheetjs.com cannot be
# reached. Git on Windows would otherwise rewrite its LF endings to CRLF on
# the next checkout — the blob in the repository stays correct, but the file
# on disk changes, and that is the file `astro build` copies into `dist/` and
# ships. The served library would then differ from the release it claims to
# be, which is the one thing a pinned vendored copy exists to prevent.
#
# `-text` means: never convert, in either direction.
public/vendor/** -text
